{"metadata":{"title":"RegexRef","externalID":"s:4GLib8RegexRefV","modules":[{"name":"GLib"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RegexRef"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"RegexRef","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RegexRef"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After instantiating a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":", you can use its methods to find matches","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"in a string, replace matches within a string, or split the string at matches.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"type":"text","text":" implements regular expression pattern matching using syntax and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semantics (such as character classes, quantifiers, and capture groups)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"similar to Perl regular expression. See the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"man:pcre2pattern(3)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for details."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A typical scenario for regex pattern matching is to check if a string","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"matches a pattern. The following statements implement this scenario."}]},{"code":["const char *regex_pattern = \".*GLib.*\";","const char *string_to_search = \"You will love the GLib implementation of regex\";","`g_autoptr(GMatchInfo)` match_info = NULL;","`g_autoptr(GRegex)` regex = NULL;","","regex = g_regex_new (regex_pattern, G_REGEX_DEFAULT, G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT, NULL);","g_assert (regex != NULL);","","if (g_regex_match (regex, string_to_search, G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT, &match_info))","  {","    int start_pos, end_pos;","    g_match_info_fetch_pos (match_info, 0, &start_pos, &end_pos);","    g_print (\"Match successful! Overall pattern matches bytes `d` to `d`\\n\", start_pos, end_pos);","  }","else","  {","    g_print (\"No match!\\n\");","  }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"{ .c }"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The constructor for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" includes two sets of bitmapped flags:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexCompileFlags","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"]—These flags"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control how GLib compiles the regex. There are options for case"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"sensitivity, multiline, ignoring whitespace, etc."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexMatchFlags"},{"text":"]—These flags control","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":"’s matching behavior, such as anchoring and customizing definitions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for newline characters.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some regex patterns include backslash assertions, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\d"},{"type":"text","text":" (digit) or"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\D"},{"type":"text","text":" (non-digit). The regex pattern must escape those backslashes. For"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"example, the pattern "},{"code":"\"\\\\d\\\\D\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" matches a digit followed by a non-digit."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"GLib’s implementation of pattern matching includes a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_position"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"argument for some of the match, replace, and split methods. Specifying"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a start position provides flexibility when you want to ignore the first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" characters of a string, but want to incorporate backslash assertions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at character "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" - 1. For example, a database field contains inconsistent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spelling for a job title: "},{"code":"healthcare provider","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"health-care provider"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The database manager wants to make the spelling consistent by adding a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyphen when it is missing. The following regex pattern tests for the string"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"care"},{"text":" preceded by a non-word boundary character (instead of a hyphen)","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and followed by a space.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"{ .c }","code":["const char *regex_pattern = \"\\\\Bcare\\\\s\";"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An efficient way to match with this pattern is to start examining at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"start_position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" 6 in the string "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"healthcare"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"health-care"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"{ .c }","code":["const char *regex_pattern = \"\\\\Bcare\\\\s\";","const char *string_to_search = \"healthcare provider\";","`g_autoptr(GMatchInfo)` match_info = NULL;","`g_autoptr(GRegex)` regex = NULL;","","regex = g_regex_new (","  regex_pattern,","  G_REGEX_DEFAULT,","  G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT,","  NULL);","g_assert (regex != NULL);","","g_regex_match_full (","  regex,","  string_to_search,","  -1,","  6, \/\/ position of 'c' in the test string.","  G_REGEX_MATCH_DEFAULT,","  &match_info,","  NULL);"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The method [method","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.Regex.match_full"},{"type":"text","text":"] (and other methods implementing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start_pos"},{"type":"text","text":") allow for lookback before the start position to determine if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the previous character satisfies an assertion.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Unless you set the [flags","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.RegexCompileFlags.RAW","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] as one of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"code":"GRegexCompileFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", all the strings passed to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" methods must","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"be encoded in UTF-8. The lengths and the positions inside the strings are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in bytes and not in characters, so, for instance, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\xc3\\xa0"},{"type":"text","text":" (i.e., "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"à"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is two bytes long but it is treated as a single character. If you set"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"G_REGEX_RAW"},{"type":"text","text":", the strings can be non-valid UTF-8 strings and a byte is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"treated as a character, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\xc3\\xa0"},{"text":" is two bytes and two characters long.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Regarding line endings, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"text":" matches a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"type":"text","text":" character, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r"},{"text":" matches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r"},{"text":" character. More generally, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\R"},{"text":" matches all typical line endings:","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"CR + LF (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r\\n"},{"type":"text","text":"), LF (linefeed, U+000A, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\n"},{"type":"text","text":"), VT (vertical tab, U+000B,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"\\v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), FF (formfeed, U+000C, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\f"},{"type":"text","text":"), CR (carriage return, U+000D, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\r"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"NEL (next line, U+0085), LS (line separator, U+2028), and PS (paragraph","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"separator, U+2029).","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The behaviour of the dot, circumflex, and dollar metacharacters are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"affected by newline characters. By default, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"type":"text","text":" matches any newline"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"character matched by "},{"code":"\\R","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". You can limit the matched newline characters by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifying the [flags"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CR","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"],"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_LF","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CRLF"},{"text":"] compile options, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with [flags","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_ANY"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CR"},{"text":"],","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"[flags"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_LF","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.RegexMatchFlags.NEWLINE_CRLF","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] match options.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"These settings are also relevant when compiling a pattern if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"[flags","type":"text"},{"code":"GLib.RegexCompileFlags.EXTENDED","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"] is set and an unescaped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"#","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" outside a character class is encountered. This indicates a comment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that lasts until after the next newline.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not modify its internal state between creation and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destruction, you can create and modify the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" instance from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"different threads. In contrast, [struct","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/MatchInfo","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"] is not thread safe.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The regular expression low-level functionalities are obtained through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the excellent "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"http:\/\/www.pcre.org\/"},{"text":" library written by Philip Hazel.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef"},{"text":" type acts as a lightweight Swift reference to an underlying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" instance.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It exposes methods that can operate on this data type through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexProtocol","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef"},{"text":" only as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unowned"},{"type":"text","text":" reference to an existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/Regex","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (instead of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":") if you want to use Automatic Reference Counting for memory management of the underlying "},{"code":"GRegex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance."}]}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GRegex"},{"text":" is a compiled form of a regular expression.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/PointerWrapper","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexProtocol"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(_:)-1hgnb","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(_:)-1vppv","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(_:)-2yoe7","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(_:)-51y4h","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(_:)-7dujh","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(cPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(constPointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(gconstpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(gpointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(mutating:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(opaquePointer:)","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/init(pattern:compileOptions:matchOptions:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/ptr"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/PointerWrapper-Implementations","doc:\/\/GLib\/documentation\/GLib\/RegexRef\/RegexProtocol-Implementations"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interface